      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"HikariStarshine\"]\n\nThis&#39;s more a question looking for clarification re: the &#39;don&#39;t post custom stuff in the forum&#39; rule than anything else...Is there a similar rule regarding showing custom content to the &gt;G guys at a con, so I&#39;d have to keep anything I came up with on my own limited to other players and any future villain contests that happen?\n\n[/quote]\n\nNot any sort of official response here, but for legal reasons I&#39;m going to bet the answer will be &quot;thanks, but no thanks.&quot; One of the big issues is, say you&#39;ve got some cool custom hero that has some gimmick where you add and remove tokens to a resource pool for various effects. Christopher sees this while working on Vengance. Then Setback come along. You could make the argument that Christopher used your design, and you&#39;re entitled to compensation for that. Sure, they can probably prove that they didn&#39;t steal it from you, but now there&#39;s all these legal hoops that could have just been avoided by not looking at outside submissions in the first place.\n",
