      "created_at": "2014-06-02T02:34:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I haven't looked at the BGG custom decks, yet. I am kind of saving that for after &gt;Games releases the last Sentinels expansion. They've said they only have two or three left. After that I figure I'll be needing a fix of new stuff at some point so I'll order the Cauldron cards or whatever there is available to keep my addiction going. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's exactly my thought, also. By then, I figure more of the bugs will be worked out of the Cauldron, too.</p>\n<p>Besides, between playtesting and just plain-old playing, I don't need more options - I can't even playtest the one villain <em><strong>I</strong></em> created!  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
